# How the mobile app is tested

{{#if mobile.android}}
## Android

{{#if mobile.real_phone}}
- **Real phone:** {{mobile.device}}, connected by cable. Controlled with **ADB** (Android's own remote
  control) and **UIAutomator** (reads every button and label on screen). Helper: `scripts/mobile/adb.sh`.
{{else}}
- **No real phone yet**, so every result comes from emulators. Say so in each report: some problems
  (camera, push notifications, performance, a maker's own Android changes) only show on real phones.
  Helper: `scripts/mobile/adb.sh`, the same commands as on a phone.
{{/if}}
- **Emulators:** {{mobile.emulators}} virtual phones on the computer, set to the same screen
  ({{mobile.width}}×{{mobile.height}} at {{mobile.dpi}} dpi){{#if mobile.real_phone}} so layout findings match the real phone{{/if}}.
  Create them once with `scripts/mobile/emulator-setup.sh create`, start them hidden with `scripts/mobile/emulator-setup.sh start`.
{{#if mobile.real_phone}}
- **Same app everywhere.** Copy the app off the real phone and install that exact file on every emulator
  (`scripts/mobile/adb.sh clone-apk`). Then all devices run identical bits.
{{else}}
- **Same app everywhere.** Install the same build file on every emulator (`scripts/mobile/adb.sh install <file.apk>`).
{{/if}}
- **One agent per device.** Two agents on one phone fight over the screen. Give each agent its own
  device id (`adb devices` lists them).
- App package: `{{mobile.package}}`

{{/if}}
{{#if mobile.ios}}
## iPhone

- **iOS Simulator** on a Mac with Xcode, model **{{mobile.ios_simulator}}**. Helper: `scripts/mobile/ios.sh`
  (screenshots, install, launch, dark mode, large text, links, fake location, push notifications).
- Install the simulator build (`.app`) the developers provide: `scripts/mobile/ios.sh install <App.app>`.
  App Store and TestFlight builds don't run on the simulator.
{{#if mobile.ios_bundle}}
- App bundle id: `{{mobile.ios_bundle}}`
{{/if}}
- **Tapping and typing** need a UI driver on iOS. Use [Maestro](https://maestro.mobile.dev) (`maestro test flow.yaml`,
  simple YAML steps) or Appium/XCUITest if the developers already have it. Keep flows in the run folder.
- Record the simulator model and iOS version with every result (`scripts/mobile/ios.sh build`).
- A real iPhone is needed for camera, Face ID, real push delivery and purchases. Those are tested by the lead
  by hand, or marked "Not covered: needs a real iPhone".

{{/if}}
## Before trusting any result

1. **Record the build**: app id, version, build number, environment, device, date.
2. **Prove the app reaches the server.** Try a login with a wrong password and look for the server's own
   error message. "No connection" means fix the setup first, not a bug.
{{#if mobile.android}}
3. **Check the right app is in front** before typing anything, especially passwords:
   `scripts/mobile/adb.sh fg`.
{{/if}}

## What to cover

- Fresh install, upgrade from the previous build, first launch
- Sent to the background and back, force-closed and reopened
- Sign out and in; the same account signed in on another device
- Forced update to a newer version, if the app has one
- No internet, slow internet, server errors
- Keyboard covering a field, scrolling to the last button{{#if mobile.android}}, system Back button{{/if}}{{#if mobile.ios}}, swipe-back gesture{{/if}}
- Dark mode, large text, long names, empty lists
- Links from emails (do they open the app or the browser?), permission denied (location, camera, notifications)
- Location-based features with a fake GPS position
- Phone turned sideways, if the app allows it
{{#if has_locales}}
- Every language ({{locales_text}}){{#if has_rtl}}, and the mirrored layout for {{rtl_text}}{{/if}}
{{/if}}
{{#if in_app_payments}}
- In-app purchases with sandbox testers: buy, cancel, restore, renew, refund
{{/if}}
{{#if has_web}}
- The same screens on the web: same data, same rules
{{/if}}

## Proof

{{#if mobile.android}}
- Android: a screenshot and a UI dump per step (`adb.sh shot <name> <dir>` and `adb.sh dump <name> <dir>`).
{{/if}}
{{#if mobile.ios}}
- iPhone: a screenshot per step (`ios.sh shot <name> <dir>`), and the Maestro flow file used.
{{/if}}
- Everything goes in the run folder, named by step.
